ot evidence for efficient synthesis from formaldehyde. V\u00e1zquez-Salazar et al. (2016, 2018) identify unstable, scarce tetroses and rapidly hydrolysing formamidine at approximately 0.30 M as serious geochemical objections. The proposed numerical window requires testing and is not attributed to Shen. Productive operation requires the measured aldehyde-forming timescale to compete with both erythrose degradation and rxn_007; no relevant rate constants are supplied.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_002\",\n      \"name\": \"Strecker formation of histidine aminonitrile\",\n      \"inputs\": [\n        \"mol_007\",\n        \"mol_003\",\n        \"mol_004\"\n      ],\n      \"outputs\": [\n        \"mol_008\",\n        \"mol_001\"\n      ],\n      \"environment\": \"Surface\",\n      \"agents\": null,\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"300-315 K, proposed screening window\",\n        \"pressure\": \"Approximately 1 bar; gas-retaining laboratory comparison required\",\n        \"catalyst\": null,\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"Anoxic and UV-shielded. Proposed pH 8.0-9.0, total HCN/CN 0.01-0.10 M, total ammonia/ammonium 0.10-1.0 M and sampling over 1-48 h. Add HCN and ammonia after the sugar\u2013amidine stage, rather than assuming all reactions are compatible simultaneously. Open-pool HCN and ammonia retention is unresolved.\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Reversible aldehyde\u2013ammonia condensation generates an imine/iminium ensemble, followed by cyanide addition. Balanced neutral-species net: C5H6N2O + CHN + NH3 -> C6H8N4 + H2O. Without an enantioselective agent, the new alpha-carbon is expected to be racemic.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Shen et al. (1990) obtained histidine after adding HCN and ammonia to the unisolated sugar\u2013amidine reaction mixture, reporting approximately 3.5% histidine relative to erythrose. That supports the overall Strecker route, but the supplied report does not establish isolation, yield or