nversion or quantify imidazolelactic acid in the Shen et al. (1990) synthesis. Cyanohydrin dissociation may instead return the aldehyde before hydrolysis. The edge is included to make a chemically credible loss channel explicit, not to claim another histidine synthesis. Its rate and product identity require experimental verification."}], "pathways": [{"pathway_id": "P1", "name": "Reported erythrose\u2013formamidine\u2013Strecker histidine route", "description": "The only histidine-producing reaction family supported experimentally by the supplied literature. Supplied D-erythrose and formamidine generate imidazole-4-acetaldehyde; HCN and ammonia permit Strecker chemistry; nitrile hydrolysis yields racemic histidine. Shen et al. (1990) support the overall laboratory endpoint at approximately 3.5% relative to erythrose, not an overall yield from formaldehyde or HCN alone. The aminonitrile and amide steps are mechanistic resolution of that route, not independently quantified demonstrations in the supplied report. The numerical surface operating windows, precursor accumulation, hydrolysis times and competitive fluxes remain unvalidated. No glycol, alcohol, hydrothermal or semi-enzymatic branch is represented as an established additional route.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_007", "mol_008", "mol_009"]}], "hub_molecules": ["mol_001", "mol_003", "mol_004", "mol_005", "mol_006", "mol_007"], "convergence_points": [{"molecule_id": "mol_001", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_005", "rxn_006"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_003", "rxn_004", "rxn_007", "rxn_009"]}, {"molecule_id": "mol_004", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_004", "rxn_007", "rxn_009"], "outgoing_reactions": ["rxn_002", "rxn_006"]}]}, "reasoning": "", "duration_ms": 309440.0177001953, "success": true, "error_message": null}
